    {
      "module": "module.aws_migrator[0]",
      "mode": "managed",
      "type": "sg_runbook_sop",
      "name": "orphan_iac_module_bootstrap",
      "provider": "provider[\"releases.stackgen.com/stackgen/stackgen\"]",
      "instances": [
        {
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "approve": true,
            "description": "# Orphans to reusable Terraform module\n\nTurn **`orphans_bundle`** — addresses that could not be hydrated into normal HCL\nroots — into a **new reusable Terraform module** (or thin wrapper), validate it,\nand hand the results back to the primary split workflow.\n\nKeywords: orphan resources, new module, terraform test, scaffold, pull request, modularization memory.\n\n## Intake\n\n1. Read `secondary_workflow_payload` / `orphans_bundle` (required inputs).\n2. Classify orphans: `network_shared`, `iam_shared`, `unmapped_vendor_resource`, `legacy_json`, `data_only`, etc.\n\n## Scaffold\n\n1. Create `modules/\u003cproposed_name\u003e/` with `main.tf`, `variables.tf`, `outputs.tf`, and a minimal `README.md` under a **writable** working directory (prefer the run working directory when the primary workdir is read-only); record the real path you used.\n2. Prefer **import blocks** pulling orphan addresses into clean resource names.\n3. Add `tests/` with `command = plan` hermetic tests.\n\n### HCL-only output (never `.tf.json`)\n\nThe module scaffold MUST be **HCL** end to end:\n\n- `main.tf` / `variables.tf` / `outputs.tf` / `versions.tf` — `.tf` only, never `*.tf.json`. `tofu fmt` is the parity check.\n- Import blocks and generator output (`tofu plan -generate-config-out=generated.tf`) — HCL.\n- `terraform show -json` snapshots are *inputs* to taxonomy decisions, never committed config.\n- If a single attribute genuinely can't be expressed in HCL, do **not** fall back to `*.tf.json` — split the address out, document it under `requires_dynamic_codegen`, and let a follow-up iteration extend the module with `dynamic { ... }` blocks or a `templatefile()` indirection (still HCL).\n\n## Validate\n\n1. `tofu fmt`, `init`, `validate`, `plan` — **one command group per step** with a conservative timeout (avoid chaining all groups through a single long-running shell line). Optional `tfsec`/`checkov` soft-fail.\n\n## Memory\n\n1. Append to a modularization memory record: the taxonomy decision tree used, naming convention, why resources were grouped together, and what still requires human ownership.\n\n## Handoff\n\n1. Open a pull request or report the module path plus test evidence. The PR path uses **`git push`** + **`gh pr create`** on the execution host, which requires a **write-scoped** git token in the environment (`GIT_TOKEN` with `repo:write` for GitHub, or the equivalent for GitLab/Bitbucket). If the read-side token lacks write scope, soft-fail the PR step and report `{stage:'memory-and-handoff', error:'git_credentials_readonly', host:...}`; do **not** ask the operator for a new token.\n2. If module registration is required, follow the org’s Terraform module registration procedure.",
            "id": "595d8575-f017-57e8-86ed-690a27f0ce71",
            "name": "aws-migrator-orphan-iac-module-bootstrap-sop",
            "status": "approved",
            "version": 1
          },
