        {
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "approve": true,
            "description": "# Reverse-engineer Terraform from allocated state\n\nReference material. Stage notes own execution.\n\nKeywords: import block, brownfield, codegen, aws.\n\n## Goal\n\nTurn each allocated state group into a readable Terraform root under\n`aws/groups/\u003cgroup_id\u003e/` with versions, providers, imports, and generated\nresource HCL. Prefer Terraform 1.5+ import blocks. Do not commit `*.tf.json`.\n\n## Entry\n\nStart from the run working directory artifacts (clone path, monolith state,\ngroup manifests, group state paths). If count reconciliation failed, do not\nscaffold HCL. Do not ask the operator for prior-phase artifacts.\n\n## Success\n\nEach group has importable HCL. Empty resource stubs are not enough. Addresses\nthat cannot be represented safely go to the orphans bundle with a short reason.\n\n## Registry fit\n\nWhen a group matches a known module, use a pinned source. Otherwise keep\nexplicit resource HCL.",
            "id": "6c598d0a-cb32-5430-af12-182cffd2e17f",
            "name": "aws-migrator-terraform-registry-reverse-iac-sop",
            "status": "approved",
            "version": 2
          },
          "sensitive_attributes": [],
          "dependencies": [
            "data.sg_guild_integration.aws",
            "data.sg_guild_integration.gcp",
            "data.sg_guild_integration.github",
            "data.sg_remote_runner.customer",
            "module.aws_migrator.module.aws_integration.sg_guild_integration.aws",
            "module.aws_migrator.module.aws_integration.sg_secret.aws_vault",
            "module.aws_migrator.module.github_integration.sg_guild_integration.github",
            "module.aws_migrator.module.github_integration.sg_secret.github_vault",
            "terraform_data.agent_stack_prerequisites",
