        {
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "approve": true,
            "description": "# Terraform validation convergence\n\nReference material. Stage notes own execution.\n\nKeywords: tofu fmt, tofu validate, tofu plan.\n\n## Goal\n\nConfirm sampled Terraform roots format and validate. A zero-change plan is\npreferred but optional for AWS discovery readiness.\n\n## Count check\n\nBefore claiming success, confirm aggregate group resource count matches the\nmonolith count. If not, stop and return to decomposition.\n\n## Per-group work\n\nFor each selected root: init, generate config when needed, format, validate,\nand optionally plan. Treat provider install failures and disk exhaustion as\nrepairable init problems: refresh the plugin cache, retry init, and record the\nfailure reason.\n\n## Looping\n\nSoft validation failures stay in the converge loop. Only a truly missing tofu\nor shell on the runner is a terminal runner block.",
