              },
              {
                "action_config": {},
                "action_type": "",
                "agent_ref": "aws-migrator-architect",
                "note": "**Upstream guard:** if `azure_source_iac_fetched` is not `\"true\"` or notes contain `blocked:azure_source_iac_fetch_failed`, record `stage_summary:azure-migration-blueprint=skipped:source_fetch_failed` and return.\n**No-approval Azure profile:** use `aws-migrator-azure-migration-profile-sop`. Do not call StackGen MCP tools, do not create AppStacks, and do not ask clarifying questions for service choices. Still investigate gaps autonomously using the approved `web_search` tool: research AWS/Azure service behavior, search Terraform Registry for AzureRM resource/data-source candidates and reusable modules, and inspect docs for the provider version pinned in each generated root. The checked-in catalog is a prior, not an exhaustive answer.\n**Incremental bring-up execution (mandatory):** `create_agent` is allowed (reactree). Put the exact BEGIN/END one-liner in CREATE_AGENT_EXPECTATION (`tool_names` only execute_series), or paste it yourself. ONE `nile-runner_execute_series` whose single command is ONLY the shell script between ---BEGIN AZURE_BLUEPRINT_EXECUTE_SERIES--- and ---END AZURE_BLUEPRINT_EXECUTE_SERIES--- below (never use the marker label as the command). Never compose your own shell.\n**Required mapping research (after the deterministic runner call):** inspect AWS `terraform.tfstate`/inventory for every unsupported, placeholder, low-confidence, or `profile_scaffold` source type. For each, use the `web_search` tool for AWS/Azure service behavior; search Terraform Registry provider/resource documentation and the dedicated Registry module search for AzureRM resources/data sources **and modules**; open docs at the `azurerm` version pinned in generated `versions.tf`. Compare required schema, observed source attributes, semantics, IAM/networking, module maintenance/source, inputs/outputs, provider constraints, and local-root composability. Do not conclude “no mapping” based only on the catalog. Create `azure/artifacts/mapping-research.md` on the remote runner using its `create_files` tool; include a candidate/disposition for every triggered source type, Registry search terms and cited URLs, the AWS evidence checked, semantic fit/mismatch, confidence, and any unresolved reason. Prefer an evidence-supported target/module, but don't force mismatched semantics or invent source values. If no gaps trigger research, still write the artifact stating the inventory/review found none. Do not record blueprint-success notes or complete this stage until the report exists and covers all triggered types; otherwise report `blocked:mapping_research_missing`.\n**Blueprint-runner evidence:** a successful runner result with `azure_migration_blueprint_ok=true` and a nonzero group count is necessary but is only the deterministic catalog baseline—not completion of this agent stage. Missing runner evidence is `stage_summary:azure-migration-blueprint=blocked:missing_runner_evidence`.\n**Research is required before stage completion:** use remote-runner `create_files` to write `azure/artifacts/mapping-research.md`. Include a disposition for every unsupported/placeholder/low-confidence/profile-only source type, including one of: cited viable resource/module plus evidence-backed fit, or checked searches/URLs plus why no defensible target exists. Research must use `web_search`, Terraform Registry provider/module search and pinned AzureRM docs, then compare candidates against actual AWS state. Empty/missing report or a missing source-type disposition is `stage_summary:azure-migration-blueprint=blocked:mapping_research_missing`. Only after report review may you note `azure_migration_blueprint_ok=true` and mark the stage `ok`. Unresolved instances remain uncovered for the 90% gate.\n**Outputs:** `azure/artifacts/migration-profile.json`, `azure/artifacts/migration-blueprint.json`, `azure/artifacts/review-needed.md`, and `azure/artifacts/mapping-research.md` (one disposition for every research-triggering source type); notes `azure_migration_blueprint_ok=true`, `azure_blueprint_group_count`, and `stage_summary:azure-migration-blueprint=ok` only when research is complete.\n\nworkflow_run_id: {{workflow_run_id}}\nWORK_ROOT: /home/runner/.{{workflow_run_id}}\nABS_WORK_ROOT: /home/runner/.{{workflow_run_id}}\nrunner_work_home: /home/runner\nremote_runner_name: nile-runner\nshell_tool_prefix: nile-runner\nscript_pack_version: 20260930.05\nscript_pack_preload_dir: /opt/aws-migrator/script-pack/20260930.05\n\n\n---BEGIN AZURE_BLUEPRINT_EXECUTE_SERIES---\nexport WORKFLOW_RUN_ID='{{workflow_run_id}}' DBSPLIT_EMBEDDED=1 GIT_TOKEN=\"${GIT_TOKEN:-${GITHUB_TOKEN:-${GH_TOKEN:-${token:-}}}}\"; export GIT_TOKEN; export GH_TOKEN=\"${GH_TOKEN:-${GIT_TOKEN}}\"; export GITHUB_TOKEN=\"${GITHUB_TOKEN:-${GIT_TOKEN}}\"; export GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0; unset AWS_PROFILE; rm -rf \"${HOME}/.aws/cli/cache\" \"${HOME}/.aws/sso\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true; echo \"aws_env_keys=$(env | grep '^AWS_' | cut -d= -f1 | tr '\\n' ' ')\"; if [ -f \"${HOME}/.aws/credentials\" ]; then echo aws_credentials_file=present; else echo aws_credentials_file=absent; fi; pack_entry(){ P='/opt/aws-migrator/script-pack/20260930.05'; if [ -x \"${P}/pack-entry.sh\" ]; then exec bash \"${P}/pack-entry.sh\" \"$@\"; fi; D=$(mktemp -d); gh release download 'pack-20260930.05' -R 'Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory' -p pack-entry.sh -D \"${D}\" \u0026\u0026 exec bash \"${D}/pack-entry.sh\" \"$@\"; }; pack_entry destination azure-migration-blueprint '{{workflow_run_id}}'\n\n---END AZURE_BLUEPRINT_EXECUTE_SERIES---\n\n",
                "parallel_agents": [],
