            "runbook_refs": [
              "aws-migrator-azure-migration-profile-sop",
              "nile-governance-learn-and-conform-sop",
              "aws-migrator-orchestration-sop",
              "aws-migrator-terraform-substate-convergence-sop"
            ],
            "stage_bindings": [
              {
                "action_config": {},
                "action_type": "",
                "agent_ref": "aws-migrator-architect",
                "note": "**Purpose:** start from an already-generated AWS IaC split branch instead of rerunning cloud2code/decomposition.\n**Handoff:** prefer workflow input / note `source_pr` (GitHub PR number) → `gh pr view` head branch; else `source_iac_branch` (default `fixture/opa-gcp-source-mini`). Optional `source_iac_repository_url` (default `https://github.com/Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory.git`).\n**Incremental bring-up execution (mandatory):** `create_agent` is allowed (reactree). Put the exact BEGIN/END one-liner in CREATE_AGENT_EXPECTATION (`tool_names` only execute_series), or paste it yourself. ONE `nile-runner_execute_series` with `commands[0].command` set to the **exact character-for-character** one-line body between `---BEGIN GCP_SOURCE_FETCH_EXECUTE_SERIES---` and `---END---` (starts with `SOURCE_PR=`, downloads `pack-entry.sh`, ends with `destination gcp-source-fetch`); set `timeout_seconds=3600` (the 30-second default killed this stage before it started in execution `0ee1ca0b`). If it still returns `signal: killed` or a deadline error, inspect `$WORK_ROOT/.work/logs/gcp-source-fetch.log` and notes, then retry the identical command once; source fetch is idempotent. That body already sets `SOURCE_PR`, `SOURCE_IAC_BRANCH`, `WORKFLOW_RUN_ID`, and `DBSPLIT_EMBEDDED=1`, and fetches the pack when `/opt` lags the module version. **FORBIDDEN (all produce empty runner output):** (1) `command=\"GCP_SOURCE_FETCH_EXECUTE_SERIES\"` (session d6e915ee); (2) `command=\"... ${GCP_SOURCE_FETCH_EXECUTE_SERIES}\"` or any `$`/`${` expansion of the label (session 93c7dc4d); (3) wrapping the label in env-prefix only; (4) rewriting the one-liner to drop `export` or hardcode an older `/opt/.../script-pack/\u003cver\u003e` path (session 55e77bfd). **RIGHT:** copy the BEGIN/END body into `commands[0].command` unchanged, except: if user input explicitly has `source_pr=\u003cdigits\u003e` or `/pull/\u003cdigits\u003e`, set only the `SOURCE_PR='…'` prefix to those digits; if user input has `source_iac_branch=…`, set only `SOURCE_IAC_BRANCH='…'` and keep `SOURCE_PR=''`. Never invent `SOURCE_PR` from examples (session eab54d0d hallucinated `34`).\n**Hard evidence gate:** completion requires a successful runner result with `gcp_source_iac_fetched=true`, `gcp_source_iac_group_count` greater than zero, and runner transcript at `$WORK_ROOT/.work/logs/gcp-source-fetch.log`. Absent those, record `stage_summary:gcp-source-fetch=blocked:missing_runner_evidence` and return blocked — and quote the runner stderr instead of inventing a silent block.\n**Discrete session notes (mandatory):** after a successful runner result you MUST `note()` each of these as its **own key** (not only an evidence blob): `gcp_source_iac_fetched`=`true`, `gcp_source_iac_group_count`=`\u003cN\u003e`, `source_iac_repository_url`, `source_iac_branch`, and `stage_summary:gcp-source-fetch`=`ok`. Downstream stages skip when these keys are missing (session 45b7206d).\n**Outputs:** `$WORK_ROOT/groups`, `$WORK_ROOT/logical_group_manifest.json`, `$WORK_ROOT/source_aws/`, plus the discrete notes above.\n**Forbidden:** cloud2code, tfstate splitting, AWS reverse-HCL hydration, StackGen MCP tools, AppStacks, or asking for the branch path.\n\nThe exact spawn context follows. Put this BEGIN/END body in CREATE_AGENT_EXPECTATION\n(or paste it yourself). Never invent a replacement command:\n\nworkflow_run_id: {{workflow_run_id}}\nWORK_ROOT: /home/runner/.{{workflow_run_id}}\nABS_WORK_ROOT: /home/runner/.{{workflow_run_id}}\nrunner_work_home: /home/runner\nremote_runner_name: nile-runner\nshell_tool_prefix: nile-runner\nscript_pack_version: 20260930.05\nscript_pack_preload_dir: /opt/aws-migrator/script-pack/20260930.05\n\ndefault_source_iac_repository_url: https://github.com/Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory.git\ndefault_source_iac_branch: fixture/opa-gcp-source-mini\ntimeout_seconds: 3600\n\n---BEGIN GCP_SOURCE_FETCH_EXECUTE_SERIES---\nexport SOURCE_PR='' SOURCE_IAC_BRANCH='fixture/opa-gcp-source-mini' WORKFLOW_RUN_ID='{{workflow_run_id}}' DBSPLIT_EMBEDDED=1 REQUIRE_GCP_LIVE_PLAN='0' GIT_TOKEN=\"${GIT_TOKEN:-${GITHUB_TOKEN:-${GH_TOKEN:-${token:-}}}}\"; export GIT_TOKEN; export GH_TOKEN=\"${GH_TOKEN:-${GIT_TOKEN}}\"; export GITHUB_TOKEN=\"${GITHUB_TOKEN:-${GIT_TOKEN}}\"; export GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0; unset AWS_PROFILE; rm -rf \"${HOME}/.aws/cli/cache\" \"${HOME}/.aws/sso\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true; echo \"aws_env_keys=$(env | grep '^AWS_' | cut -d= -f1 | tr '\\n' ' ')\"; if [ -f \"${HOME}/.aws/credentials\" ]; then echo aws_credentials_file=present; else echo aws_credentials_file=absent; fi; pack_entry(){ P='/opt/aws-migrator/script-pack/20260930.05'; if [ -x \"${P}/pack-entry.sh\" ]; then exec bash \"${P}/pack-entry.sh\" \"$@\"; fi; D=$(mktemp -d); gh release download 'pack-20260930.05' -R 'Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory' -p pack-entry.sh -D \"${D}\" \u0026\u0026 exec bash \"${D}/pack-entry.sh\" \"$@\"; }; pack_entry destination gcp-source-fetch '{{workflow_run_id}}'\n\n---END GCP_SOURCE_FETCH_EXECUTE_SERIES---\n\n",
                "parallel_agents": [],
                "runbook_refs": [
                  "aws-migrator-azure-migration-profile-sop",
                  "aws-migrator-orchestration-sop"
                ],
                "skill_refs": [
                  "aws-migrator-azure-migration-profile-sop",
                  "aws-migrator-orchestration-sop"
                ],
                "spawn_contracts": [],
                "stage_depends_on": [],
                "stage_id": "gcp-source-fetch"
              },
              {
                "action_config": {},
                "action_type": "",
                "agent_ref": "aws-migrator-architect",
                "note": "**Upstream guard:** skip only when notes clearly show fetch failure (`blocked:gcp_source_iac_fetch_failed` or `stage_summary:gcp-source-fetch=blocked:`). If any note content contains `gcp_source_iac_fetched=true` (including inside `gcp-source-fetch-evidence`), treat upstream as OK and run this stage — do not invent `skipped:source_fetch_failed`.\n**No-approval GCP profile:** use `aws-migrator-azure-migration-profile-sop`. Do not call StackGen MCP tools, do not create AppStacks, and do not ask clarifying questions for service choices. This does not mean “catalog only”: research unknown/low-confidence AWS→GCP mappings using source evidence and Terraform Registry/provider docs as described by `mapping-provider-schema-reasoning`. The mapping catalog is a starting point, not an exhaustive map; do not invent a new static mapping without verifying target semantics and the pinned Google provider schema.\n**Incremental bring-up execution (mandatory):** Your FIRST tool call must be ONE `nile-runner_execute_series` with `commands[0].command` set to the **exact character-for-character** one-line body between `---BEGIN GCP_BLUEPRINT_EXECUTE_SERIES---` and `---END---` (starts with `WORKFLOW_RUN_ID=`, downloads `pack-entry.sh`, ends with `destination gcp-migration-blueprint`). **FORBIDDEN:** `command=\"GCP_BLUEPRINT_EXECUTE_SERIES\"` or any `$`/`${` expansion of the label; do not rewrite the pack path. If the lead agent cannot call the runner tool directly, spawn one subagent whose sole goal is to paste that BEGIN/END body once — never skip the runner.\n**Mapping research:** before finalizing the blueprint, identify unsupported, placeholder, low-confidence, or profile-only decisions. Use `web_search` to look up AWS service semantics; search Terraform Registry provider/resource documentation and the dedicated Terraform Registry module search for Google provider resources/data sources **and reusable modules**. Inspect exact-version Google provider docs for each root and pin any selected module/provider version. For modules, inspect source/inputs/outputs/provider constraints and verify local-root compatibility; do not treat a search result or module name as proof. Compare candidates against the actual AWS state attributes/service behavior. Record resource/module addresses and versions, search terms, URLs, source evidence, semantic fit/mismatches, confidence, and unresolved decisions in `gcp/artifacts/mapping-research.md`. Prefer evidence-backed targets over copying the catalog, but do not force a mapping if semantics do not fit. Preserve source-instance reconciliation and describe unresolved instances honestly.\n**Blueprint-runner evidence:** a successful runner result with `gcp_migration_blueprint_ok=true` and a nonzero group count is necessary but only gives the deterministic catalog baseline—not completion of this agent stage. Missing runner evidence is `stage_summary:gcp-migration-blueprint=blocked:missing_runner_evidence`.\n**Research is required before stage completion:** use remote-runner `create_files` to write `gcp/artifacts/mapping-research.md`. Include a disposition for every unsupported/placeholder/low-confidence/profile-only source type: either a cited viable provider resource/module candidate with evidence-backed fit, or the searches/URLs checked and why no defensible target fits. Actively use `web_search`, Terraform Registry provider/module search, pinned Google provider docs, and actual AWS source-state attributes/relationships; don't stop at the checked-in catalog. Inspect candidate module source, version, inputs/outputs, provider constraints, and local-root composition before recommending one. Empty/missing research or a missing per-source disposition is `stage_summary:gcp-migration-blueprint=blocked:mapping_research_missing`. Inspect and enrich the blueprint from evidence when a candidate is supportable; keep unresolved resources explicitly uncovered. Only after reviewing the artifact and blueprint may you note `gcp_migration_blueprint_ok=true` and mark the stage `ok`.\n**Outputs:** `gcp/artifacts/migration-profile.json`, `gcp/artifacts/migration-blueprint.json`, `gcp/artifacts/review-needed.md`, `gcp/artifacts/mapping-research.md` (one disposition per research-triggering source type), plus the discrete notes above only when research is complete.\n\nworkflow_run_id: {{workflow_run_id}}\nWORK_ROOT: /home/runner/.{{workflow_run_id}}\nABS_WORK_ROOT: /home/runner/.{{workflow_run_id}}\nrunner_work_home: /home/runner\nremote_runner_name: nile-runner\nshell_tool_prefix: nile-runner\nscript_pack_version: 20260930.05\nscript_pack_preload_dir: /opt/aws-migrator/script-pack/20260930.05\n\n\n---BEGIN GCP_BLUEPRINT_EXECUTE_SERIES---\nexport WORKFLOW_RUN_ID='{{workflow_run_id}}' DBSPLIT_EMBEDDED=1 GIT_TOKEN=\"${GIT_TOKEN:-${GITHUB_TOKEN:-${GH_TOKEN:-${token:-}}}}\"; export GIT_TOKEN; export GH_TOKEN=\"${GH_TOKEN:-${GIT_TOKEN}}\"; export GITHUB_TOKEN=\"${GITHUB_TOKEN:-${GIT_TOKEN}}\"; export GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0; unset AWS_PROFILE; rm -rf \"${HOME}/.aws/cli/cache\" \"${HOME}/.aws/sso\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true; echo \"aws_env_keys=$(env | grep '^AWS_' | cut -d= -f1 | tr '\\n' ' ')\"; if [ -f \"${HOME}/.aws/credentials\" ]; then echo aws_credentials_file=present; else echo aws_credentials_file=absent; fi; pack_entry(){ P='/opt/aws-migrator/script-pack/20260930.05'; if [ -x \"${P}/pack-entry.sh\" ]; then exec bash \"${P}/pack-entry.sh\" \"$@\"; fi; D=$(mktemp -d); gh release download 'pack-20260930.05' -R 'Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory' -p pack-entry.sh -D \"${D}\" \u0026\u0026 exec bash \"${D}/pack-entry.sh\" \"$@\"; }; pack_entry destination gcp-migration-blueprint '{{workflow_run_id}}'\n\n---END GCP_BLUEPRINT_EXECUTE_SERIES---\n\n",
