    {
      "module": "module.governance_codify[0]",
      "mode": "managed",
      "type": "sg_runbook_sop",
      "name": "governance_opa_codify_method",
      "provider": "provider[\"releases.stackgen.com/stackgen/stackgen\"]",
      "instances": [
        {
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "approve": true,
            "description": "# Governance markdown → IaC OPA codify method\n\nUse this skill in **`rules-codify`** after intake recorded `codify_inventory_json`.\n\nLocal OPA validation is **optional** in the GitHub sidecar (opa is usually absent). Write packs, commit, push, open PR — **rules-validate** GitHub Actions is the authoritative gate.\n\n## Goal (non-negotiable)\n\nWrite **conftest/OPA policies that evaluate Terraform plan JSON** (output of `terraform show -json` / `tofu show -json`).\n\n- **Input root:** `input.resource_changes` and/or `input.planned_values` / `input.configuration`.\n- **Deny when IaC violates** a markdown obligation (missing tags, bad labels, forbidden attributes, etc.).\n- **Forbidden:** inventing process schemas (`input.exception`, `input.resource.phase`, `input.resource.human_approval`, readiness booleans). Those are not Terraform plan fields.\n- **Process-only markdown** (exception authority, approval authority, evidence schema as process): put obligations in `controls.json` with `\"enforce\": false` and **do not** write `policy.rego` (or write an empty pack with no deny rules and note why). Do **not** invent fake JSON APIs for process docs.\n\n## Classify each markdown doc\n\n| Class | Examples | Action |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **IaC-enforceable** | tagging/labeling, GCP org policy constraints, resource encryption/network/IAM requirements stated as resource properties | `enforce: true` + Rego over `resource_changes` |\n| **Process / authority** | exception authority, approval routing, evidence review flow, human-review mandates | `enforce: false` only — no process Rego |\n| **Mixed** | production-readiness / priority controls | Enforce only obligations that map to **resource attributes in a plan**; leave human-approval/evidence-traceability as `enforce: false` |\n\n## Parallel codify (mandatory when `stale_docs` has 2+ entries)\n\nYou are the **coordinator**. Do not codify every doc yourself in series when multiple stale docs exist.\n\n### Coordinator sequence\n\n1. `read_notes` → parse `codify_inventory_json`.\n2. `load_skill(governance-opa-codify-method)` (this file).\n3. **Bootstrap + branch** (parent only): run CODIFY_BRANCH execute_series; bootstrap when `bootstrap_needed=true`. Sub-agents assume branch + clones already exist.\n4. **Assign work units** from `stale_docs[]` — one sub-agent per markdown file (or per folder when multiple stale docs share a directory).\n5. **Spawn all pack workers synchronously in one LLM turn** — `create_agent` once per work unit in the **same response**. Set `background=false` (default). **Wait for every TOOL_CALL_RESULT** before merging manifest. Never fire-and-forget pack workers.\n6. Collect `codify_pack_\u003cslug\u003e` notes from completed workers only.\n7. Parent merges `rules/manifest.json`, commits, `note(codify_rules_written=true)` + `note(codify_handoff_json=...)`.\n\nNever spawn a sub-agent whose goal includes `rules-pr`, push, or PR creation.\n\n**Forbidden:** one monolithic sub-agent (`codify-bootstrap-branch-and-workers`) that does all packs.\n\n### Planner vs pack-worker split\n\n| Who | Job |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Stage planner** | Bootstrap/branch sub-agent, then N parallel pack workers in one response; merge manifest. |\n| **Bootstrap sub-agent** | Scaffold via **create_files** + branch `{source_commit_sha}_{YYYYMMDDHHMMSS}` only. tool_names MUST include `cloud-github_create_files`. |\n| **Pack-worker** | Read markdown → classify → `controls.json` → **IaC** `policy.rego` (if any enforce:true) → tests + terraform-shaped fixtures. |\n\n### Sub-agent budget (minimum per pack worker)\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| `task_type` | `tool_calling` |\n| `max_tool_iterations` | **32** |\n| `max_llm_calls` | **40** |\n| `tool_names` | `cloud-github_create_files`, `cloud-github_execute_command`, `cloud-github_execute_series`, `note`, `read_notes`, `load_skill` |\n\nNo nested `create_agent` in pack workers.\n\n### Sub-agent goal template\n\n```text\nIaC OPA pack worker for ONE governance markdown file. rules-codify only — no PR.\n\nSource: /tmp/governance-source/\u003cDOC_PATH\u003e\nTarget pack: /tmp/governance-codify/\u003cPACK_DIR\u003e/\ncontent_sha256: \u003cSHA256\u003e\n\n1. load_skill(governance-opa-codify-method)\n2. cat the markdown. Classify IaC-enforceable vs process-only.\n3. Write controls.json. Only set enforce:true for obligations checkable on Terraform plan JSON.\n4. If any enforce:true: write policy.rego that iterates input.resource_changes (and tags/labels/attributes). FORBIDDEN: input.exception, input.resource.phase, invented process flags.\n5. policy_test.rego + conftest fixtures that LOOK LIKE terraform show -json (resource_changes with type, name, change.after.tags|labels).\n6. If `command -v opa` succeeds: run `opa test /tmp/governance-codify/\u003cPACK_DIR\u003e` and set `opa_test_passed` true/false. If opa is **not** on PATH (expected in GitHub sidecar): set `opa_test_passed=skipped_local`, note why, and **continue** — do NOT fail the worker. CI validates on the PR.\n7. If zero IaC-enforceable controls: controls.json only (all enforce:false); skip policy.rego; note iac_enforceable=false.\n8. Do NOT edit manifest or git commit. note(codify_pack_\u003cSLUG\u003e=JSON) with keys: doc_path, pack_dir, content_sha256, controls_count, enforce_count, iac_enforceable, policy_written, opa_test_passed.\n```\n\n## Per stale doc\n\n### 1. Read markdown\n\n```bash\ncat /tmp/governance-source/\u003cdoc_path\u003e\n```\n\nExtract: purpose, scope, MUST/SHALL, tables of required tags/labels/attributes, advisory vs blocking.\n\n### 2. `controls.json`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema\": \"nile-governance-controls/v1\",\n  \"source_paths\": [\"governance/tagging-labeling-standard.md\"],\n  \"summary\": \"Enforces required Azure tags and GCP labels on Terraform planned resources.\",\n  \"input_schema\": {\n    \"description\": \"Terraform plan JSON (terraform show -json). Policies read resource_changes[].change.after.\",\n    \"required_fields\": [\"resource_changes\"]\n  },\n  \"controls\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TLS-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Azure required tags present\",\n      \"source_section\": \"Section 5 – Azure Required Tags\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"obligation\": \"Nile-managed Azure resources must contain all required tags.\",\n      \"enforce\": true,\n      \"iac_check\": \"resource_changes for azurerm_* create/update; after.tags must include required keys\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### 3. `policy.rego` (IaC only)\n\n**Package name is mandatory:** `package policy` (CI evaluates `data.policy.deny`).\n\n```rego\npackage policy\n\nimport rego.v1\n\n# governance/tagging-labeling-standard.md § Section 5 – Azure Required Tags\n# TLS-001: Nile-managed Azure resources must contain all required tags.\n\ndefault allow := true\n\nrequired_azure_tags := {\"owner\", \"created-by\", \"cost-center\", \"environment\", \"function\", \"service\", \"repo\", \"applicationname\", \"name\", \"notificationdistlist\", \"ssp\", \"trproductid\", \"apmid\"}\n\nnonempty(s) if {\n\tis_string(s)\n\ttrim(s, \" \\t\\n\\r\") != \"\"\n}\n\ndeny contains msg if {\n\tsome rc in input.resource_changes\n\tstartswith(rc.type, \"azurerm_\")\n\trc.change.actions[_] in {\"create\", \"update\"}\n\ttags := object.get(rc.change.after, \"tags\", {})\n\tsome required in required_azure_tags\n\tnot nonempty(object.get(tags, required, \"\"))\n\tmsg := sprintf(\"TLS-001: %s.%s missing required Azure tag %q\", [rc.type, rc.name, required])\n}\n```\n\nEvery `deny` must:\n\n1. Cite markdown path + section in a comment.\n2. Include control id in `msg`.\n3. Inspect **plan** fields (`resource_changes`, `type`, `change.after`, `tags`, `labels`, …).\n\n### Rego syntax rules (OPA 1.x — fail CI if violated)\n\n| Do | Do not |\n| --- | --- |\n| `package policy` | `package nile.codify` or other names |\n| `trim(s, \" \\t\\n\\r\")` (cutset required) | `trim(s)` |\n| Partial set: `vals contains x if { ... }` with **separate** rules, no `else` | `vals(after) contains x if {..} else contains y if {..}` |\n| Tests in `package policy` with `count(deny) == 0 with input as plan` | `count(data.policy.deny with input as plan)` (with inside count arg) |\n| Real Terraform attrs (`tags`, `labels`, `location`, `network_interface`) | Invented attrs (`logging_enabled`, `phase`, `human_approval`) |\n\n### 4. `policy_test.rego` (copy this shape)\n\n```rego\npackage policy\n\nimport rego.v1\n\npass_plan := {\n\t\"resource_changes\": [{\n\t\t\"address\": \"azurerm_resource_group.ok\",\n\t\t\"mode\": \"managed\",\n\t\t\"type\": \"azurerm_resource_group\",\n\t\t\"name\": \"ok\",\n\t\t\"change\": {\"actions\": [\"create\"], \"after\": {\"tags\": {\"owner\": \"platform\", \"created-by\": \"ci\", \"cost-center\": \"cc\", \"environment\": \"dev\", \"function\": \"app\", \"service\": \"nile\", \"repo\": \"org/repo\", \"applicationname\": \"demo\", \"name\": \"ok\", \"notificationdistlist\": \"ops\", \"ssp\": \"ssp\", \"trproductid\": \"tr\", \"apmid\": \"apm\"}}},\n\t}],\n}\n\nfail_plan := {\n\t\"resource_changes\": [{\n\t\t\"address\": \"azurerm_resource_group.bad\",\n\t\t\"mode\": \"managed\",\n\t\t\"type\": \"azurerm_resource_group\",\n\t\t\"name\": \"bad\",\n\t\t\"change\": {\"actions\": [\"create\"], \"after\": {\"tags\": {\"owner\": \"\"}}},\n\t}],\n}\n\ntest_pass_no_deny if {\n\tcount(deny) == 0 with input as pass_plan\n}\n\ntest_fail_has_deny if {\n\tcount(deny) \u003e 0 with input as fail_plan\n}\n```\n\n**Wrong (parse error):** `count(data.policy.deny with input as pass_plan) == 0`\n\n**Right:** `count(deny) == 0 with input as pass_plan` (same package) or `count(policy.deny) == 0 with input as pass_plan` from `package policy_test`.\n\nAfter writing files, run when opa is available:\n\n```bash\ncommand -v opa \u0026\u0026 opa test /tmp/governance-codify/\u003cPACK_DIR\u003e\n```\n\nWhen opa is absent in the GitHub sidecar, skip local test and set `opa_test_passed=skipped_local`. CI validates on the PR. When opa is present, fix until PASS before noting success.\n\n### 5. Conftest fixtures (must be terraform plan shaped)\n\n`conftest/fixtures/pass/plan.json` / `fail/plan.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"format_version\": \"1.2\",\n  \"terraform_version\": \"1.5.0\",\n  \"resource_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"address\": \"azurerm_resource_group.example\",\n      \"mode\": \"managed\",\n      \"type\": \"azurerm_resource_group\",\n      \"name\": \"example\",\n      \"provider_name\": \"registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/azurerm\",\n      \"change\": {\n        \"actions\": [\"create\"],\n        \"after\": {\n          \"name\": \"rg-example\",\n          \"location\": \"eastus\",\n          \"tags\": {\n            \"owner\": \"platform\",\n            \"created-by\": \"pipeline\",\n            \"cost-center\": \"cc-1\",\n            \"environment\": \"dev\",\n            \"function\": \"app\",\n            \"service\": \"nile\",\n            \"repo\": \"org/repo\",\n            \"applicationname\": \"demo\",\n            \"name\": \"rg-example\",\n            \"notificationdistlist\": \"ops@example.com\",\n            \"ssp\": \"ssp-1\",\n            \"trproductid\": \"tr-1\",\n            \"apmid\": \"apm-1\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nFail fixture: same shape with missing/empty tags or labels.\n\n**Reject** fixtures whose root is `exception`, `resource.phase`, or other non-plan objects.\n\n### 6. Manifest\n\nParent merges entries after workers finish. Sub-agents do not edit manifest.\n\n## Bootstrap (when `bootstrap_needed=true` OR scaffold files missing)\n\nWrite scaffold with **cloud-github_create_files** (absolute paths under /tmp/governance-codify). Never invent YAML/shell via execute_series heredocs.\nRequired paths: rules/README.md, rules/manifest.json (only if absent), rules/run-tests.sh, .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml.\nUse exact content from the BOOTSTRAP FILES block in this SOP. FORBIDDEN: conftest-action, instrumenta/conftest, or hand-written workflow differing from bootstrap.\nAfter create_files succeeds, commit with ONE execute_series (git only — no heredocs):\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 git add rules .github \u0026\u0026 git diff --cached --quiet || git commit -m \"codify: sync rules validation scaffold\"\nFallback only if create_files unavailable: ONE execute_series (python bootstrap — verbatim, no heredocs):\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\nimport base64\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nroot = Path(\".\")\n(root / \"rules\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n(root / \".github/workflows\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\nreadme = \"# Nile governance OPA rules\\n\\nTerraform-plan OPA policies under rules/.\\n\"\n(root / \"rules/README.md\").write_text(readme)\n\nmanifest_path = root / \"rules/manifest.json\"\nif not manifest_path.exists():\n    manifest_path.write_text('{\\n  \"schema\": \"nile-codify-manifest/v1\",\\n  \"entries\": []\\n}\\n')\n\nrun_tests = base64.b64decode(\"{{RULES_RUN_TESTS_SH_B64}}\")\n(root / \"rules/run-tests.sh\").write_bytes(run_tests)\n(root / \"rules/run-tests.sh\").chmod(0o755)\n\nworkflow = base64.b64decode(\"{{GITHUB_RULES_VALIDATE_B64}}\")\n(root / \".github/workflows/rules-validate.yml\").write_bytes(workflow)\nprint(\"bootstrap_scaffold_ok\")\nPY\nchmod +x rules/run-tests.sh\ngit add rules .github\nif git diff --cached --quiet; then echo \"bootstrap_scaffold_unchanged\"; else git commit -m \"codify: sync rules validation scaffold\"; fi\n\n**BOOTSTRAP FILES** content is in `governance-rules-codify-sop` — write with create_files, not shell.\n\nWhen opa is absent in the GitHub sidecar, **skip** local `run-tests.sh`. Ensure scaffold files exist, merge manifest, commit, and hand off. CI runs `run-tests.sh` on the PR branch.\n\n## Quality bar (fail the stage if violated)\n\n- Every `enforce: true` control has Rego that reads `input.resource_changes` (or equivalent plan paths).\n- Zero process-schema denies (`input.exception`, invented readiness flags).\n- Fixtures are terraform plan JSON; pass fixture → no deny; fail fixture → deny.\n- Local `opa test` may be skipped in the sidecar (`opa_test_passed=skipped_local`); CI must pass for packs with `policy.rego`.\n- `rules/run-tests.sh` and `.github/workflows/rules-validate.yml` exist on the branch.\n- Process-only docs: `enforce_count=0`, `iac_enforceable=false`, no fake Rego.\n- Prefer strong packs for **tagging-labeling-standard** and cloud policy/resource docs.",
            "id": "b62474b7-5062-529c-960d-2c26788ba24d",
            "name": "governance-opa-codify-method",
            "status": "approved",
            "version": 7
          },
          "sensitive_attributes": [],
          "dependencies": [
            "data.sg_guild_integration.github",
            "terraform_data.agent_stack_prerequisites",
            "terraform_data.governance_codify_prerequisites"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "module.governance_codify[0]",
      "mode": "managed",
      "type": "sg_runbook_sop",
      "name": "governance_rules_codify",
      "provider": "provider[\"releases.stackgen.com/stackgen/stackgen\"]",
      "instances": [
        {
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "approve": true,
            "description": "# Governance rules codify\n\nConvert living governance **markdown** (source repo) into durable **IaC OPA/conftest** packs under `rules/` (target repo). Enforceable Rego must evaluate **Terraform plan JSON** (`resource_changes`). Process-only obligations stay in `controls.json` with `\"enforce\": false` — never invent `input.exception` schemas. Validation runs in **target-repo GitHub Actions**.\n\nLocal OPA validation is **optional** in the GitHub sidecar (opa is usually absent). Write packs, commit, push, open PR — **rules-validate** GitHub Actions is the authoritative gate.\n\nLoad **`governance-opa-codify-method`** during `rules-codify` for the IaC markdown→Rego method.\n\n## Cross-repo model (mandatory)\n\n| Role | Default repo | Clone dir | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Source** | `Walmart-StackGen/Governance-and-Policy` @ `main` | `/tmp/governance-source` | Read `governance/**/*.md` (markdown only) |\n| **Target** | `Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory` @ `main` | `/tmp/governance-codify` | Write `rules/**`, open PR, run CI |\n\nNever read policy markdown from the target clone. Never write Rego to the source clone.\n\n## Tooling boundary\n\n- **Allowed:** `cloud-github_create_files`, `cloud-github_execute_command`, `cloud-github_execute_series`, `gh`, `git`, `rg`, `note`, `read_notes`, `load_skill`, `create_agent` (reactree, **current stage scope only**)\n- **Forbidden:** sub-agents whose goal is a **later workflow stage** (e.g. \"do codify and PR\"), remote-runner tools, shell heredocs for file content\n\nAuth probe: `gh api user -q .login` before mutations.\n\n## Integration shell policy (mandatory)\n\nThe GitHub sidecar blocks **environment enumeration**. Never run: `env`, `printenv`, bare `export`, bare `set`, `set foo`.\n\n**Safe patterns:** `export NAME=value \u0026\u0026 ...`, `set -eu`, `gh`, `git`, `rg`, `jq`, `mktemp`, `printf`, `cd`.\n\n## Integration shell recovery (mandatory when tools fail)\n\nThe GitHub sidecar blocks **environment enumeration** and shell-based file authoring patterns.\n\n**Never:** `env`, `printenv`, bare `export`, bare `set`, `cat \u003c\u003cEOF` / heredoc file writes, or inventing scaffold YAML in execute_series.\n\n**When execute_series returns `command blocked`:** do not fail the stage. Switch strategy:\n1. Scaffold/workflow files → **create_files** with absolute paths (primary).\n2. Git commit/push only → minimal execute_series with **git/gh only** (no file content in shell).\n3. Retry once with the approved python bootstrap script (verbatim) if create_files is insufficient.\n\n**When scaffold is missing at PR time:** create_files + git commit before declaring blocked. Only fail closed after create_files AND git commit both fail.\n\n## Dual clone (mandatory)\n\nIntake FIRST tool call — ONE `cloud-github_execute_series` (copy verbatim):\n\n---BEGIN CODIFY_INTAKE_EXECUTE_SERIES---\nset -eu; SRC='{{SOURCE_DIR}}'; TGT='{{TARGET_DIR}}'; SRC_REPO='{{SOURCE_REPO}}'; TGT_REPO='{{TARGET_REPO}}'; SRC_REF='{{SOURCE_REF}}'; TGT_REF='{{TARGET_REF}}'; sync_repo(){ local repo=\"$1\" dir=\"$2\" ref=\"$3\"; if git -C \"$dir\" rev-parse HEAD \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then git -C \"$dir\" fetch origin \"$ref\" --depth=1 \u0026\u0026 git -C \"$dir\" checkout \"$ref\" \u0026\u0026 git -C \"$dir\" reset --hard \"origin/$ref\"; else rm -rf \"$dir\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true; gh repo clone \"$repo\" \"$dir\" -- --branch \"$ref\" --single-branch --depth 1; fi; git -C \"$dir\" rev-parse HEAD; }; sync_repo \"$SRC_REPO\" \"$SRC\" \"$SRC_REF\"; sync_repo \"$TGT_REPO\" \"$TGT\" \"$TGT_REF\"\n---END CODIFY_INTAKE_EXECUTE_SERIES---\n\nThen note:\n\n- `note(codify_source_clone_dir=/tmp/governance-source)`\n- `note(codify_source_repo_full=Walmart-StackGen/Governance-and-Policy)`\n- `note(codify_source_ref=main)`\n- `note(codify_clone_dir=/tmp/governance-codify)` (target; legacy key name)\n- `note(codify_repo_full=Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory)` (target PR repo)\n- `note(codify_target_ref=main)`\n\nAll **`create_files`** paths must be absolute under **`/tmp/governance-codify/...`**.\n\n## File writes (mandatory)\n\nUse **`cloud-github_create_files`** with **absolute paths** under the **target** clone:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"/tmp/governance-codify/rules/manifest.json\",\n      \"content\": \"{ … valid nile-codify-manifest/v1 … }\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nRelative paths like `rules/README.md` **fail** in this integration. Never use heredoc/`tee`/`cat \u003e` in shell.\n\nAfter writes: `git add … \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"codify: …\"` from **target** clone root (`working_dir=/tmp/governance-codify`).\n\n## Inputs (workflow notes or defaults)\n\n| Input | Default |\n| --- | --- |\n| `source_repository_url` | `https://github.com/Walmart-StackGen/Governance-and-Policy.git` |\n| `source_ref` | `main` |\n| `target_repository_url` | `https://github.com/Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory.git` |\n| `target_ref` | `main` |\n| `base_branch` | `main` (PR base on **target** repo) |\n| `rules_output_dir` | `rules` |\n| `force_recodify` | false |\n\n## Intake (`rules-intake`)\n\n1. Dual clone with CODIFY_INTAKE execute_series (see above).\n2. On **source** clone: glob `governance/**/*.md` (and `architecture/**/*.md` if present). Hash each file.\n3. On **target** clone: read `rules/manifest.json` if present; check bootstrap (`run-tests.sh`, `rules-validate` workflow).\n4. Compute stale docs: source markdown hash vs manifest entries on **target**.\n5. `note(codify_inventory_json=\u003cnile-codify-inventory/v1\u003e)`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"$id\": \"nile-codify-inventory/v1\",\n  \"title\": \"Governance codify intake inventory\",\n  \"description\": \"Emitted by rules-intake: cross-repo inventory — source markdown vs target rules/manifest.json.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"schema\",\n    \"source_repo\",\n    \"source_ref\",\n    \"source_commit_sha\",\n    \"repo\",\n    \"ref\",\n    \"commit_sha\",\n    \"stale_docs\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"schema\": { \"const\": \"nile-codify-inventory/v1\" },\n    \"source_repo\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"owner/repo for governance markdown (e.g. Walmart-StackGen/Governance-and-Policy)\"\n    },\n    \"source_ref\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Git ref cloned on the source repo\"\n    },\n    \"source_commit_sha\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"HEAD SHA of the source clone at intake\"\n    },\n    \"repo\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"owner/repo for Rego output and PR (target, e.g. Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory)\"\n    },\n    \"ref\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Git ref cloned on the target repo before branching\"\n    },\n    \"commit_sha\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"HEAD SHA of the target clone at intake\"\n    },\n    \"rules_output_dir\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"default\": \"rules\"\n    },\n    \"bootstrap_needed\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"True when target rules/run-tests.sh or rules-validate GHA workflow is missing\"\n    },\n    \"force_recodify\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n    \"stale_docs\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"required\": [\"doc_path\", \"content_sha256\", \"reason\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"doc_path\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Path in the source repo (e.g. governance/priority-controls.md)\"\n          },\n          \"content_sha256\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^[a-f0-9]{64}$\"\n          },\n          \"reason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\"missing_pack\", \"hash_mismatch\", \"force_recodify\"]\n          },\n          \"existing_pack_dir\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Pack dir under target rules/ if present\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"unchanged_docs\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nInventory must include **both** `source_repo`/`source_ref` and target `repo`/`ref`. `doc_path` values are paths **in the source repo** (e.g. `governance/priority-controls.md`).\n\n6. **Stop.** Do not write Rego or spawn codify/PR sub-agents — `rules-codify` runs next.\n\n## Codify (`rules-codify`) — OPA expert stage\n\nLoad skill **`governance-opa-codify-method`** first.\n\nSkip when zero stale docs and not `force_recodify` — `note(codify_skipped_unchanged=true)` and stop.\n\n### Parallel fan-out (mandatory when 2+ stale docs)\n\n1. Parent: bootstrap (if needed) + create branch on target.\n2. Build work units from `stale_docs[]` — **one sub-agent per markdown file**, or **one sub-agent per folder**.\n3. Call **`create_agent` for every work unit in the same LLM response**.\n4. Each pack worker: classify IaC vs process; write `controls.json`; for IaC controls write Rego over `input.resource_changes` + terraform-shaped fixtures. **No process-schema Rego.** No manifest/commit in workers.\n5. Parent: merge manifest, commit, `note(codify_handoff_json=...)`.\n\nSub-agent minimum budget: `max_tool_iterations=24`, `max_llm_calls=30`. No nested `create_agent`.\n\n### Single stale doc\n\nWhen only one stale doc, codify inline (no sub-agent) using the steps below.\n\nFor each stale doc (inline or sub-agent):\n\n1. **Read** `/tmp/governance-source/\u003cdoc_path\u003e` (full markdown).\n2. **Extract essence** — obligations, priorities, blocking language → `controls.json`.\n3. **Write OPA** — `policy.rego` (Rego v1), `policy_test.rego`, conftest pass/fail fixtures on **target** only.\n4. **Update** `rules/manifest.json` `entries[]`; **commit** on target.\n\n### Branch (on target)\n\nBranch name pattern: **`{source_commit_sha}_{YYYYMMDDHHMMSS}`** (full source SHA + UTC timestamp — unique every run).\n\nONE `cloud-github_execute_series` — substitute `SOURCE_COMMIT_SHA` with **full** `source_commit_sha` from `codify_inventory_json`:\n\n---BEGIN CODIFY_BRANCH_EXECUTE_SERIES---\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 git fetch origin {{BASE_BRANCH}} \u0026\u0026 SOURCE_SHA='SOURCE_COMMIT_SHA' \u0026\u0026 DATE=$(date -u +%Y%m%d%H%M%S) \u0026\u0026 BRANCH=\"${SOURCE_SHA}_${DATE}\" \u0026\u0026 git checkout -b \"${BRANCH}\" origin/{{BASE_BRANCH}} \u0026\u0026 printf 'codify_branch=%s\\n' \"${BRANCH}\"\n---END CODIFY_BRANCH_EXECUTE_SERIES---\n\nExample: `f8f6f171a0a15c195954c53c330e15df2af6aa99_20260827153000`\n\n`note(codify_branch=\u003cbranch from stdout\u003e)`.\n\n### Bootstrap first (when bootstrap_needed=true OR scaffold missing on target)\n\nWrite scaffold with **cloud-github_create_files** (absolute paths under /tmp/governance-codify). Never invent YAML/shell via execute_series heredocs.\nRequired paths: rules/README.md, rules/manifest.json (only if absent), rules/run-tests.sh, .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml.\nUse exact content from the BOOTSTRAP FILES block in this SOP. FORBIDDEN: conftest-action, instrumenta/conftest, or hand-written workflow differing from bootstrap.\nAfter create_files succeeds, commit with ONE execute_series (git only — no heredocs):\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 git add rules .github \u0026\u0026 git diff --cached --quiet || git commit -m \"codify: sync rules validation scaffold\"\nFallback only if create_files unavailable: ONE execute_series (python bootstrap — verbatim, no heredocs):\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\nimport base64\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nroot = Path(\".\")\n(root / \"rules\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n(root / \".github/workflows\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\nreadme = \"# Nile governance OPA rules\\n\\nTerraform-plan OPA policies under rules/.\\n\"\n(root / \"rules/README.md\").write_text(readme)\n\nmanifest_path = root / \"rules/manifest.json\"\nif not manifest_path.exists():\n    manifest_path.write_text('{\\n  \"schema\": \"nile-codify-manifest/v1\",\\n  \"entries\": []\\n}\\n')\n\nrun_tests = base64.b64decode(\"{{RULES_RUN_TESTS_SH_B64}}\")\n(root / \"rules/run-tests.sh\").write_bytes(run_tests)\n(root / \"rules/run-tests.sh\").chmod(0o755)\n\nworkflow = base64.b64decode(\"{{GITHUB_RULES_VALIDATE_B64}}\")\n(root / \".github/workflows/rules-validate.yml\").write_bytes(workflow)\nprint(\"bootstrap_scaffold_ok\")\nPY\nchmod +x rules/run-tests.sh\ngit add rules .github\nif git diff --cached --quiet; then echo \"bootstrap_scaffold_unchanged\"; else git commit -m \"codify: sync rules validation scaffold\"; fi\n\n**BOOTSTRAP FILES** — write via `cloud-github_create_files` (absolute paths):\n\n- `/tmp/governance-codify/rules/README.md` — short intro (IaC OPA policies for Terraform plan JSON)\n- `/tmp/governance-codify/rules/manifest.json` — schema **nile-codify-manifest/v1**, `\"entries\": []` only when file absent\n- `/tmp/governance-codify/rules/run-tests.sh` — verbatim:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Validates Nile governance OPA packs against Terraform plan fixtures.\n# Policy package MUST be: package policy  (deny contains msg if { ... })\nset -euo pipefail\n\nrepo_root=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" \u0026\u0026 pwd)\"\nstatus=0\n\nif ! command -v opa \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then\n  echo \"opa not found on PATH\" \u003e\u00262\n  exit 1\nfi\n\npolicy_count=0\nwhile IFS= read -r policy_file; do\n  [ -n \"$policy_file\" ] || continue\n  policy_count=$((policy_count + 1))\n  pack_dir=\"$(dirname \"$policy_file\")\"\n  echo \"=== opa test ${pack_dir} ===\"\n  if [ ! -f \"${pack_dir}/policy_test.rego\" ]; then\n    echo \"missing policy_test.rego in ${pack_dir}\" \u003e\u00262\n    status=1\n    continue\n  fi\n  if ! opa test \"${pack_dir}\"; then\n    echo \"opa test failed: ${pack_dir}\" \u003e\u00262\n    status=1\n    continue\n  fi\n\n  pass_fixture=\"${pack_dir}/conftest/fixtures/pass/plan.json\"\n  fail_fixture=\"${pack_dir}/conftest/fixtures/fail/plan.json\"\n\n  if [ -f \"$pass_fixture\" ]; then\n    echo \"=== pass fixture ${pass_fixture} ===\"\n    pass_denies=\"$(opa eval -f raw -i \"$pass_fixture\" -d \"${pack_dir}/policy.rego\" 'data.policy.deny' || true)\"\n    if [ \"$pass_denies\" != \"[]\" ]; then\n      echo \"expected no denies on pass fixture, got: ${pass_denies}\" \u003e\u00262\n      status=1\n    fi\n  fi\n\n  if [ -f \"$fail_fixture\" ]; then\n    echo \"=== fail fixture ${fail_fixture} ===\"\n    fail_denies=\"$(opa eval -f raw -i \"$fail_fixture\" -d \"${pack_dir}/policy.rego\" 'data.policy.deny' || true)\"\n    if [ -z \"$fail_denies\" ] || [ \"$fail_denies\" = \"[]\" ] || [ \"$fail_denies\" = \"undefined\" ]; then\n      echo \"expected denies on fail fixture, got: ${fail_denies}\" \u003e\u00262\n      status=1\n    fi\n  fi\ndone \u003c \u003c(find \"$repo_root/rules\" -name 'policy.rego' -type f | sort)\n\nif [ \"$policy_count\" -eq 0 ]; then\n  echo \"No policy.rego files under rules/ — nothing to validate\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n\nexit \"$status\"\n```\n\n- `/tmp/governance-codify/.github/workflows/rules-validate.yml` — verbatim:\n\n```yaml\nname: rules-validate\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n    paths:\n      - \"rules/**\"\n      - \".github/workflows/rules-validate.yml\"\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n    paths:\n      - \"rules/**\"\n      - \".github/workflows/rules-validate.yml\"\n\njobs:\n  rules-validate:\n    name: rules-validate\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Install opa\n        run: |\n          curl -sL -o opa https://openpolicyagent.org/downloads/v1.4.2/opa_linux_amd64_static\n          chmod +x opa\n          sudo mv opa /usr/local/bin/opa\n          opa version\n\n      - name: Validate manifest schema\n        run: |\n          python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\n          import json\n          from pathlib import Path\n          p = Path(\"rules/manifest.json\")\n          assert p.exists(), \"rules/manifest.json missing\"\n          manifest = json.loads(p.read_text())\n          assert manifest.get(\"schema\") == \"nile-codify-manifest/v1\", manifest.get(\"schema\")\n          assert isinstance(manifest.get(\"entries\"), list), \"entries must be a list\"\n          print(f\"manifest ok entries={len(manifest['entries'])}\")\n          PY\n\n      - name: Run rules test harness\n        run: bash rules/run-tests.sh\n```\n\nVerify with ONE execute_series (read-only check):\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 missing=0; test -f rules/run-tests.sh || missing=1; test -f .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml || missing=1; if test -f .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml \u0026\u0026 grep -q conftest-action .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml; then missing=1; fi; echo \"scaffold_missing=$missing\"\n\n**Before handoff:** skip local `run-tests.sh` when opa is absent in the sidecar. Merge manifest, commit, push, and write top-level handoff notes. CI validates on the PR.\n\n### Per stale doc (mandatory when stale_docs non-empty)\n\nMap source path to target pack dir — drop `.md`, prefix with `rules/`:\n\n```text\nSource: governance/priority-controls.md\nTarget: rules/governance/priority-controls/\n  controls.json\n  policy.rego\n  policy_test.rego\n  conftest/fixtures/pass/plan.json\n  conftest/fixtures/fail/plan.json\n```\n\n**controls.json** must validate against leaf shape; cite `source_paths` pointing at **source repo** paths.\n\n**manifest.json** on **target** must use `\"entries\"` array (not `\"packs\"`). Update after each pack.\n\nCommit per pack on **target**. `note(codify_rules_written=true)` after `git log origin/\u003cbase\u003e..HEAD` shows commits.\n\n### Stage handoff (required before stage ends)\n\nCopy values from sub-agents to **top-level** note keys. Keys prefixed `subagent:` are **not** visible to `rules-pr`.\n\n```text\nnote(codify_branch=\u003cbranch name\u003e)\nnote(codify_bootstrap_done=true)   # when bootstrap ran\nnote(codify_rules_written=true)\nnote(codify_branch_pushed=true)    # after push to origin\nnote(codify_handoff_json=\u003cJSON string\u003e)\n```\n\nJSON must include: `source_clone_dir`, `clone_dir` (target), `repo_full` (target), `source_repo_full`, `branch`, `commit_sha`, `rules_written` (bool), `manifest_path` (`rules/manifest.json`).\n\nBefore `rules-codify` ends — verify branch exists on origin (substitute CODIFY_BRANCH):\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 BR='CODIFY_BRANCH' \u0026\u0026 git fetch origin \"$BR\" --depth=1 \u0026\u0026 if git rev-parse \"origin/$BR\" \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then ahead=$(git rev-list --count \"origin/{{BASE_BRANCH}}..origin/$BR\" 2\u003e/dev/null || echo 0); echo \"codify_branch_on_origin=1\"; echo \"codify_branch_ahead=$ahead\"; else echo codify_branch_on_origin=0; exit 1; fi\nMust print `codify_branch_on_origin=1` and `codify_branch_ahead` \u003e 0. If verify fails: push branch, then write top-level notes:\nnote(codify_branch=...), note(codify_branch_pushed=true), note(codify_handoff_json=...).\n\n**Never delegate `rules-pr` or \"remaining stages\" to create_agent** — stagerunner runs the next stage.\n\n## PR + CI gate (`rules-pr`) — mandatory deliverable\n\n### Recover state (mandatory first actions)\n\n## Handoff recovery (mandatory when notes are empty)\n\n`workflow_notes_snapshot` may arrive with `\"notes\":{}`. Subagent-scoped keys (`subagent:*`, nested prefixes) are **not** visible to `rules-pr`. Do **not** fail immediately.\n\n**Recovery ladder (run in order, stop when `codify_branch` is known):**\n\n1. `read_notes` — use top-level `codify_branch`, `codify_handoff_json`, or `codify_inventory_json.source_commit_sha`.\n2. If still missing: ONE cloud-github_execute_series (git-only branch discovery — verbatim, substitute SOURCE_COMMIT_SHA from inventory when known):\n   cd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 BASE='{{BASE_BRANCH}}' \u0026\u0026 REPO='{{TARGET_REPO}}' \u0026\u0026 PREF='SOURCE_COMMIT_SHA' \u0026\u0026 if ! git rev-parse HEAD \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then rm -rf ./* ./.[!.]* 2\u003e/dev/null || true; gh repo clone \"$REPO\" . -- --branch \"$BASE\" --single-branch --depth 1; fi \u0026\u0026 git fetch origin --prune \"$BASE\" \u0026\u0026 best= \u0026\u0026 best_ts=0 \u0026\u0026 for b in $(git for-each-ref --format='%(refname:strip=3)' refs/remotes/origin); do echo \"$b\" | grep -Eq '^[0-9a-f]{40}_[0-9]{14}$' || continue; if [ -n \"$PREF\" ] \u0026\u0026 [ \"$PREF\" != 'SOURCE_COMMIT_SHA' ]; then case \"$b\" in \"$PREF\"_*) ;; *) continue ;; esac; fi; ahead=$(git rev-list --count \"origin/$BASE..origin/$b\" 2\u003e/dev/null || echo 0); if [ \"$ahead\" -gt 0 ]; then ts=${b#*_}; if [ \"$ts\" -gt \"$best_ts\" ]; then best_ts=$ts; best=$b; fi; fi; done \u0026\u0026 if [ -z \"$best\" ]; then echo codify_branch=; echo codify_branch_recover=failed; exit 1; fi \u0026\u0026 printf 'codify_branch=%s\\n' \"$best\" \u0026\u0026 printf 'codify_branch_ahead=%s\\n' \"$(git rev-list --count \"origin/$BASE..origin/$best\")\" \u0026\u0026 echo codify_branch_recover=ok\n3. Parse stdout `codify_branch=...`. Immediately `note(codify_branch=\u003cvalue\u003e)` at **top level** (required for downstream tools).\n4. If recover script prints `codify_branch_recover=failed`: fail closed with `blocked:codify_pr_failed` only after step 2.\n\n**Then** checkout branch (verbatim, substitute CODIFY_BRANCH):\nset -eu; TGT='{{TARGET_DIR}}'; TGT_REPO='{{TARGET_REPO}}'; BRANCH='CODIFY_BRANCH'; if git -C \"$TGT\" rev-parse HEAD \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then git -C \"$TGT\" fetch origin \"$BRANCH\" --depth=1 \u0026\u0026 git -C \"$TGT\" checkout \"$BRANCH\"; else rm -rf \"$TGT\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true; gh repo clone \"$TGT_REPO\" \"$TGT\" -- --branch \"$BRANCH\" --single-branch --depth 1; fi; git -C \"$TGT\" rev-parse HEAD \u0026\u0026 git -C \"$TGT\" log --oneline -1\n\nFORBIDDEN: declaring `blocked:codify_pr_failed` because `workflow_notes_snapshot.notes` is empty without running branch recovery first.\n\n1. `read_notes` and parse `[Workflow notes from prior stage]` / `workflow_notes_snapshot` footer (may be empty — use recovery ladder above).\n2. Target clone is `/tmp/governance-codify`. PR repo is **target** (`Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory`).\n3. After recovery: `note(codify_branch=\u003cbranch\u003e)` at top level before checkout or PR.\n4. If `codify_blocked_status` or branch recovery failed with zero commits ahead of base, fail closed with `blocked:codify_pr_failed`.\n\nOpen PR on **target repo** when the codify branch has commits ahead of base.\n\n**Preflight (mandatory before push):**\n\n1. Check scaffold: ONE execute_series (verbatim):\n   cd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 missing=0; test -f rules/run-tests.sh || missing=1; test -f .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml || missing=1; if test -f .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml \u0026\u0026 grep -q conftest-action .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml; then missing=1; fi; echo \"scaffold_missing=$missing\"\n2. If `scaffold_missing=1` or workflow contains `conftest-action`: Write scaffold with **cloud-github_create_files** (absolute paths under /tmp/governance-codify). Never invent YAML/shell via execute_series heredocs.\nRequired paths: rules/README.md, rules/manifest.json (only if absent), rules/run-tests.sh, .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml.\nUse exact content from the BOOTSTRAP FILES block in this SOP. FORBIDDEN: conftest-action, instrumenta/conftest, or hand-written workflow differing from bootstrap., then git commit:\n   cd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 git add rules .github \u0026\u0026 git diff --cached --quiet || git commit -m \"codify: sync rules validation scaffold\"\n   Do **not** fail with `blocked:codify_pr_failed` until create_files + git commit were attempted. On `command blocked`, use create_files (not shell heredocs).\n2. Skip local `run-tests.sh` preflight (opa not in GitHub sidecar). Open the PR, then run the CI wait+self-heal loop until `rules-validate` is green.\n\n### Push + PR (first tool call after preflight)\n\nONE `cloud-github_execute_series` (`working_dir=/tmp/governance-codify`, `timeout_seconds=600`):\n\n---BEGIN CODIFY_PR_EXECUTE_SERIES---\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 BRANCH='{{BRANCH}}' \u0026\u0026 if git ls-remote --exit-code --heads origin \"${BRANCH}\" \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then BRANCH=\"${BRANCH}-$(date -u +%H%M%S)\"; git branch -m \"${BRANCH}\"; fi \u0026\u0026 git push -u origin \"${BRANCH}\" \u0026\u0026 gh pr create --repo {{OWNER}}/{{REPO}} --base {{BASE_BRANCH}} --head \"${BRANCH}\" --title \"{{PR_TITLE}}\" --body \"{{PR_BODY_LINE1}}. {{PR_BODY_LINE2}}. Created using [StackGen](https://ai.stackgen.com)\"\n---END CODIFY_PR_EXECUTE_SERIES---\n\nSubstitute target `OWNER/REPO`, `BRANCH`, title/body. Capture PR URL from stdout.\n\n`note(rules_pr_url=\u003curl\u003e)`, `note(codify_pr_opened=true)`.\n\n### CI gate (wait + self-heal — mandatory)\n\n### CI wait + self-heal loop (mandatory — do not stop at first red check)\n\nAfter PR is open and `note(rules_pr_url=\u003curl\u003e)`, run up to 5 repair cycles:\n\n**Cycle (repeat until green or max iterations):**\n\n1. Resolve PR number from `rules_pr_url` (or `gh pr list --repo Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory --head \u003ccodify_branch\u003e --json number -q '.[0].number'`).\n2. ONE cloud-github_execute_series (timeout_seconds=900, working_dir=/tmp/governance-codify) — copy verbatim, substitute CODIFY_PR_NUMBER:\nset -eu\nREPO='{{TARGET_REPO}}'\nPR='{{PR_NUMBER}}'\nCHECK='{{CHECK_NAME}}'\nTIMEOUT='{{CI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS}}'\nCLONE='{{CLONE_DIR}}'\nelapsed=0\ninterval=25\necho \"ci_gate: waiting for $CHECK on $REPO#$PR (timeout=${TIMEOUT}s)\"\nwhile [ \"$elapsed\" -lt \"$TIMEOUT\" ]; do\n  checks=\"$(gh pr checks \"$PR\" --repo \"$REPO\" 2\u003e\u00261 || true)\"\n  echo \"$checks\"\n  if printf '%s\\n' \"$checks\" | awk -v c=\"$CHECK\" '$1==c \u0026\u0026 $2==\"pass\"{ok=1} END{exit !ok}'; then\n    echo \"codify_ci_status=green\"\n    exit 0\n  fi\n  if printf '%s\\n' \"$checks\" | awk -v c=\"$CHECK\" '$1==c \u0026\u0026 ($2==\"fail\" || $2==\"failure\"){bad=1} END{exit !bad}'; then\n    echo \"codify_ci_status=failed\"\n    break\n  fi\n  pending=0\n  if printf '%s\\n' \"$checks\" | awk -v c=\"$CHECK\" '$1==c \u0026\u0026 ($2==\"pending\" || $2==\"in_progress\" || $2==\"queued\"){pending=1} END{exit !pending}'; then\n    pending=1\n  fi\n  if [ \"$pending\" -eq 0 ] \u0026\u0026 printf '%s\\n' \"$checks\" | grep -q \"$CHECK\"; then\n    :\n  fi\n  sleep \"$interval\"\n  elapsed=$((elapsed + interval))\ndone\nif [ \"$elapsed\" -ge \"$TIMEOUT\" ]; then\n  echo \"codify_ci_status=timeout\"\nfi\nHEAD=\"$(gh pr view \"$PR\" --repo \"$REPO\" --json headRefName -q .headRefName)\"\nRUN_ID=\"$(gh run list --repo \"$REPO\" --branch \"$HEAD\" --workflow rules-validate.yml --limit 5 --json databaseId,conclusion -q '.[0].databaseId' 2\u003e/dev/null || true)\"\necho \"=== ci_failed_logs run_id=${RUN_ID} branch=${HEAD} ===\"\nif [ -n \"$RUN_ID\" ] \u0026\u0026 [ \"$RUN_ID\" != \"null\" ]; then\n  gh run view \"$RUN_ID\" --repo \"$REPO\" --log-failed 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -400 || true\nfi\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$checks\" \u003e /tmp/codify-ci-checks.txt\nexit 1\n3. If stdout contains `codify_ci_status=green` → `note(codify_ci_green=true)`, `note(rules_codify_ok=true)`, stop.\n4. If failed: read failed logs from stdout. Classify and fix on branch (then push):\n   - **Scaffold/workflow** (`conftest`, `no files found`, missing `run-tests.sh`, wrong workflow): Write scaffold with **cloud-github_create_files** (absolute paths under /tmp/governance-codify). Never invent YAML/shell via execute_series heredocs.\nRequired paths: rules/README.md, rules/manifest.json (only if absent), rules/run-tests.sh, .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml.\nUse exact content from the BOOTSTRAP FILES block in this SOP. FORBIDDEN: conftest-action, instrumenta/conftest, or hand-written workflow differing from bootstrap. then git commit (verbatim):\n     cd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 git add rules .github \u0026\u0026 git diff --cached --quiet || git commit -m \"codify: sync rules validation scaffold\"\n   - **opa test** failure naming a pack dir: fix `policy.rego` / `policy_test.rego` / fixtures via create_files (absolute paths under /tmp/governance-codify).\n   - **manifest** validation: fix `rules/manifest.json` schema/entries.\n5. Push repair commit — ONE execute_series (substitute CODIFY_BRANCH):\n   cd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 BRANCH='{{BRANCH}}' \u0026\u0026 git add -A \u0026\u0026 if git diff --cached --quiet; then echo \"ci_repair_nothing_to_push\"; exit 0; fi \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"{{COMMIT_MSG}}\" \u0026\u0026 git push origin \"$BRANCH\" \u0026\u0026 git rev-parse HEAD\n6. `note(codify_ci_iteration=\u003cn\u003e)` with failure summary; loop to step 1.\n\nFORBIDDEN: parsing `gh pr checks --json` (often empty). Use the CI gate script table output only.\nFORBIDDEN: shell heredocs (`cat \u003c\u003c`) for scaffold files — use create_files.\nAfter 5 failed cycles → `blocked:codify_ci_failed` with last log excerpt. Do NOT merge.\n\nDo **not** merge.\n\n## Blocked sentinels\n\n| Sentinel | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `blocked:github_integration_unavailable` | gh auth down |\n| `blocked:codify_source_unavailable` | cannot read source or target repo |\n| `blocked:codify_pr_failed` | push or PR create failed on **target** |\n| `blocked:codify_tests_failed` | local `run-tests.sh` failed when `require_local_opa_validation=true` |\n| `blocked:codify_ci_failed` | `rules-validate` failed |\n\n## Forbidden\n\n- Sub-agents that skip ahead to later workflow stages\n- Relative paths in `create_files`\n- Writing Rego to the source repo or reading policy only from target\n- Invented process Rego (`input.exception`, `input.resource.phase`, fake approval flags)\n- Invented controls; fake PR URLs; merge without human approval\n- Scaffold-only commits with no real IaC `policy.rego` when tagging/resource docs are stale\n- Conftest fixtures that are not Terraform plan JSON\n- `instrumenta/conftest-action` or hand-written `rules-validate.yml` that differs from bootstrap verbatim\n- Parsing `gh pr checks --json` instead of the CI gate script; stopping at first red check without repair loop\n- Shell heredocs (`cat \u003c\u003c`) for scaffold or workflow files — use create_files instead\n- Failing a stage on first `command blocked` without retrying via create_files or git-only commands\n- Declaring `blocked:codify_pr_failed` when `workflow_notes_snapshot.notes` is empty without running branch recovery first",
