                "stage_id": "rules-intake"
              },
              {
                "action_config": {},
                "action_type": "",
                "agent_ref": "governance-codify-architect",
                "note": "You are the OPA/Rego coordinator. read_notes + load_skill(governance-opa-codify-method) first.\n\nGitHub sidecar /tmp is NOT durable across stages. FIRST tool call — re-sync clones (copy verbatim, same as intake):\nset -eu; SRC='{{SOURCE_DIR}}'; TGT='{{TARGET_DIR}}'; SRC_REPO='{{SOURCE_REPO}}'; TGT_REPO='{{TARGET_REPO}}'; SRC_REF='{{SOURCE_REF}}'; TGT_REF='{{TARGET_REF}}'; sync_repo(){ local repo=\"$1\" dir=\"$2\" ref=\"$3\"; if git -C \"$dir\" rev-parse HEAD \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then git -C \"$dir\" fetch origin \"$ref\" --depth=1 \u0026\u0026 git -C \"$dir\" checkout \"$ref\" \u0026\u0026 git -C \"$dir\" reset --hard \"origin/$ref\"; else rm -rf \"$dir\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true; gh repo clone \"$repo\" \"$dir\" -- --branch \"$ref\" --single-branch --depth 1; fi; git -C \"$dir\" rev-parse HEAD; }; sync_repo \"$SRC_REPO\" \"$SRC\" \"$SRC_REF\"; sync_repo \"$TGT_REPO\" \"$TGT\" \"$TGT_REF\"\n\nParse codify_inventory_json. Parent-only: bootstrap when bootstrap_needed=true, then branch:\nONE cloud-github_execute_series (replace SOURCE_COMMIT_SHA with full source_commit_sha from inventory):\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 git fetch origin {{BASE_BRANCH}} \u0026\u0026 SOURCE_SHA='SOURCE_COMMIT_SHA' \u0026\u0026 DATE=$(date -u +%Y%m%d%H%M%S) \u0026\u0026 BRANCH=\"${SOURCE_SHA}_${DATE}\" \u0026\u0026 git checkout -b \"${BRANCH}\" origin/{{BASE_BRANCH}} \u0026\u0026 printf 'codify_branch=%s\\n' \"${BRANCH}\"\nBranch pattern: {source_commit_sha}_{YYYYMMDDHHMMSS} (UTC timestamp — unique per run). note(codify_branch=\u003cfrom stdout\u003e).\n\nPARALLEL CODIFY (mandatory when stale_docs has 2+ entries):\n- Do NOT spawn one mega sub-agent for all packs.\n- Sequence: (1) bootstrap/branch sub-agent and WAIT for result, (2) YOU spawn create_agent once per stale doc in ONE response with background=false.\n- Bootstrap sub-agent tool_names MUST include cloud-github_create_files (scaffold via create_files, not shell heredocs).\n- WAIT for every pack-worker TOOL_CALL_RESULT before merging manifest. Do not start rules-pr logic.\n- Each pack worker MUST write IaC Rego (input.resource_changes) for enforce:true. FORBIDDEN process schemas.\n- Local opa test is optional in the GitHub sidecar. If opa missing: set opa_test_passed=skipped_local in codify_pack_* JSON and continue. CI is authoritative.\n- trim() always needs cutset: trim(s, \" \\\\t\\\\n\\\\r\"). Never trim(s).\n- Prefer tagging-labeling-standard with azurerm_/google_ resource_changes fixtures.\n- Process-only docs: controls.json enforce:false only.\n- ALWAYS write rules/run-tests.sh + .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml if missing via create_files (BOOTSTRAP FILES in SOP — never shell heredocs).\n- Do **not** fail the stage because `opa` or `run-tests.sh` is missing locally. After manifest merge + commit, hand off and push. CI runs `run-tests.sh` on the PR.\n- Budget per pack worker: max_tool_iterations=32, max_llm_calls=40, timeout_seconds\u003e=900.\n- Parent: merge manifest from completed codify_pack_* notes only, commit on /tmp/governance-codify.\n\nWhen force_recodify=true: treat all docs as stale and overwrite packs.\n\nMANDATORY top-level notes before rules-codify ends (subagent: keys are NOT visible to rules-pr):\n- note(codify_branch=\u003cbranch name\u003e)\n- note(codify_bootstrap_done=true) when bootstrap ran\n- note(codify_rules_written=true) after commits on branch\n- note(codify_branch_pushed=true) after push succeeds\n- note(codify_handoff_json=\u003cJSON with branch, commit_sha, repo_full, rules_written\u003e)\n\nBefore `rules-codify` ends — verify branch exists on origin (substitute CODIFY_BRANCH):\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 BR='CODIFY_BRANCH' \u0026\u0026 git fetch origin \"$BR\" --depth=1 \u0026\u0026 if git rev-parse \"origin/$BR\" \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then ahead=$(git rev-list --count \"origin/{{BASE_BRANCH}}..origin/$BR\" 2\u003e/dev/null || echo 0); echo \"codify_branch_on_origin=1\"; echo \"codify_branch_ahead=$ahead\"; else echo codify_branch_on_origin=0; exit 1; fi\nMust print `codify_branch_on_origin=1` and `codify_branch_ahead` \u003e 0. If verify fails: push branch, then write top-level notes:\nnote(codify_branch=...), note(codify_branch_pushed=true), note(codify_handoff_json=...).\n\nMANDATORY before stage ends — push branch to origin (substitute CODIFY_BRANCH with codify_branch from notes):\nONE cloud-github_execute_series working_dir=/tmp/governance-codify:\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 git push -u origin {{BRANCH}}\n\nNever delegate rules-pr. End with note(codify_rules_written=true), note(codify_branch_pushed=true), and note(codify_handoff_json=...).\n",
