                "agent_ref": "governance-codify-architect",
                "note": "read_notes + workflow_notes_snapshot. PR only — no Rego authoring in this stage.\nIf spawning a sub-agent for PR/CI, tool_names MUST include cloud-github_create_files.\n\nPR repo: TARGET Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory. Clone dir /tmp/governance-codify.\n\n## Handoff recovery (mandatory when notes are empty)\n\n`workflow_notes_snapshot` may arrive with `\"notes\":{}`. Subagent-scoped keys (`subagent:*`, nested prefixes) are **not** visible to `rules-pr`. Do **not** fail immediately.\n\n**Recovery ladder (run in order, stop when `codify_branch` is known):**\n\n1. `read_notes` — use top-level `codify_branch`, `codify_handoff_json`, or `codify_inventory_json.source_commit_sha`.\n2. If still missing: ONE cloud-github_execute_series (git-only branch discovery — verbatim, substitute SOURCE_COMMIT_SHA from inventory when known):\n   cd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 BASE='{{BASE_BRANCH}}' \u0026\u0026 REPO='{{TARGET_REPO}}' \u0026\u0026 PREF='SOURCE_COMMIT_SHA' \u0026\u0026 if ! git rev-parse HEAD \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then rm -rf ./* ./.[!.]* 2\u003e/dev/null || true; gh repo clone \"$REPO\" . -- --branch \"$BASE\" --single-branch --depth 1; fi \u0026\u0026 git fetch origin --prune \"$BASE\" \u0026\u0026 best= \u0026\u0026 best_ts=0 \u0026\u0026 for b in $(git for-each-ref --format='%(refname:strip=3)' refs/remotes/origin); do echo \"$b\" | grep -Eq '^[0-9a-f]{40}_[0-9]{14}$' || continue; if [ -n \"$PREF\" ] \u0026\u0026 [ \"$PREF\" != 'SOURCE_COMMIT_SHA' ]; then case \"$b\" in \"$PREF\"_*) ;; *) continue ;; esac; fi; ahead=$(git rev-list --count \"origin/$BASE..origin/$b\" 2\u003e/dev/null || echo 0); if [ \"$ahead\" -gt 0 ]; then ts=${b#*_}; if [ \"$ts\" -gt \"$best_ts\" ]; then best_ts=$ts; best=$b; fi; fi; done \u0026\u0026 if [ -z \"$best\" ]; then echo codify_branch=; echo codify_branch_recover=failed; exit 1; fi \u0026\u0026 printf 'codify_branch=%s\\n' \"$best\" \u0026\u0026 printf 'codify_branch_ahead=%s\\n' \"$(git rev-list --count \"origin/$BASE..origin/$best\")\" \u0026\u0026 echo codify_branch_recover=ok\n3. Parse stdout `codify_branch=...`. Immediately `note(codify_branch=\u003cvalue\u003e)` at **top level** (required for downstream tools).\n4. If recover script prints `codify_branch_recover=failed`: fail closed with `blocked:codify_pr_failed` only after step 2.\n\n**Then** checkout branch (verbatim, substitute CODIFY_BRANCH):\nset -eu; TGT='{{TARGET_DIR}}'; TGT_REPO='{{TARGET_REPO}}'; BRANCH='CODIFY_BRANCH'; if git -C \"$TGT\" rev-parse HEAD \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then git -C \"$TGT\" fetch origin \"$BRANCH\" --depth=1 \u0026\u0026 git -C \"$TGT\" checkout \"$BRANCH\"; else rm -rf \"$TGT\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true; gh repo clone \"$TGT_REPO\" \"$TGT\" -- --branch \"$BRANCH\" --single-branch --depth 1; fi; git -C \"$TGT\" rev-parse HEAD \u0026\u0026 git -C \"$TGT\" log --oneline -1\n\nFORBIDDEN: declaring `blocked:codify_pr_failed` because `workflow_notes_snapshot.notes` is empty without running branch recovery first.\n\nIf branch has 0 commits ahead of base after recovery+checkout, fail closed with blocked:codify_pr_failed — do not open empty PR.\n\nPREFLIGHT before push:\n1) Check scaffold (verbatim): cd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 missing=0; test -f rules/run-tests.sh || missing=1; test -f .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml || missing=1; if test -f .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml \u0026\u0026 grep -q conftest-action .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml; then missing=1; fi; echo \"scaffold_missing=$missing\"\n2) If scaffold_missing=1 or conftest-action in workflow: create_files (absolute paths, BOOTSTRAP FILES in SOP) then git commit:\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 git add rules .github \u0026\u0026 git diff --cached --quiet || git commit -m \"codify: sync rules validation scaffold\"\nOn command blocked: switch to create_files — never shell heredocs. Do not fail blocked:codify_pr_failed until create_files + commit tried.\n2) Skip local run-tests.sh. Open PR, then CI wait+self-heal loop until \"rules-validate\" green.\n\nTHEN: ONE cloud-github_execute_series (working_dir=/tmp/governance-codify, timeout_seconds=600):\ncd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 BRANCH='{{BRANCH}}' \u0026\u0026 if git ls-remote --exit-code --heads origin \"${BRANCH}\" \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then BRANCH=\"${BRANCH}-$(date -u +%H%M%S)\"; git branch -m \"${BRANCH}\"; fi \u0026\u0026 git push -u origin \"${BRANCH}\" \u0026\u0026 gh pr create --repo {{OWNER}}/{{REPO}} --base {{BASE_BRANCH}} --head \"${BRANCH}\" --title \"{{PR_TITLE}}\" --body \"{{PR_BODY_LINE1}}. {{PR_BODY_LINE2}}. Created using [StackGen](https://ai.stackgen.com)\"\nSubstitute {{BRANCH}} with codify_branch from notes. note(rules_pr_url=\u003cfrom gh stdout\u003e).\n\n### CI wait + self-heal loop (mandatory — do not stop at first red check)\n\nAfter PR is open and `note(rules_pr_url=\u003curl\u003e)`, run up to 5 repair cycles:\n\n**Cycle (repeat until green or max iterations):**\n\n1. Resolve PR number from `rules_pr_url` (or `gh pr list --repo Walmart-StackGen/Nile-Factory --head \u003ccodify_branch\u003e --json number -q '.[0].number'`).\n2. ONE cloud-github_execute_series (timeout_seconds=900, working_dir=/tmp/governance-codify) — copy verbatim, substitute CODIFY_PR_NUMBER:\nset -eu\nREPO='{{TARGET_REPO}}'\nPR='{{PR_NUMBER}}'\nCHECK='{{CHECK_NAME}}'\nTIMEOUT='{{CI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS}}'\nCLONE='{{CLONE_DIR}}'\nelapsed=0\ninterval=25\necho \"ci_gate: waiting for $CHECK on $REPO#$PR (timeout=${TIMEOUT}s)\"\nwhile [ \"$elapsed\" -lt \"$TIMEOUT\" ]; do\n  checks=\"$(gh pr checks \"$PR\" --repo \"$REPO\" 2\u003e\u00261 || true)\"\n  echo \"$checks\"\n  if printf '%s\\n' \"$checks\" | awk -v c=\"$CHECK\" '$1==c \u0026\u0026 $2==\"pass\"{ok=1} END{exit !ok}'; then\n    echo \"codify_ci_status=green\"\n    exit 0\n  fi\n  if printf '%s\\n' \"$checks\" | awk -v c=\"$CHECK\" '$1==c \u0026\u0026 ($2==\"fail\" || $2==\"failure\"){bad=1} END{exit !bad}'; then\n    echo \"codify_ci_status=failed\"\n    break\n  fi\n  pending=0\n  if printf '%s\\n' \"$checks\" | awk -v c=\"$CHECK\" '$1==c \u0026\u0026 ($2==\"pending\" || $2==\"in_progress\" || $2==\"queued\"){pending=1} END{exit !pending}'; then\n    pending=1\n  fi\n  if [ \"$pending\" -eq 0 ] \u0026\u0026 printf '%s\\n' \"$checks\" | grep -q \"$CHECK\"; then\n    :\n  fi\n  sleep \"$interval\"\n  elapsed=$((elapsed + interval))\ndone\nif [ \"$elapsed\" -ge \"$TIMEOUT\" ]; then\n  echo \"codify_ci_status=timeout\"\nfi\nHEAD=\"$(gh pr view \"$PR\" --repo \"$REPO\" --json headRefName -q .headRefName)\"\nRUN_ID=\"$(gh run list --repo \"$REPO\" --branch \"$HEAD\" --workflow rules-validate.yml --limit 5 --json databaseId,conclusion -q '.[0].databaseId' 2\u003e/dev/null || true)\"\necho \"=== ci_failed_logs run_id=${RUN_ID} branch=${HEAD} ===\"\nif [ -n \"$RUN_ID\" ] \u0026\u0026 [ \"$RUN_ID\" != \"null\" ]; then\n  gh run view \"$RUN_ID\" --repo \"$REPO\" --log-failed 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -400 || true\nfi\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$checks\" \u003e /tmp/codify-ci-checks.txt\nexit 1\n3. If stdout contains `codify_ci_status=green` → `note(codify_ci_green=true)`, `note(rules_codify_ok=true)`, stop.\n4. If failed: read failed logs from stdout. Classify and fix on branch (then push):\n   - **Scaffold/workflow** (`conftest`, `no files found`, missing `run-tests.sh`, wrong workflow): Write scaffold with **cloud-github_create_files** (absolute paths under /tmp/governance-codify). Never invent YAML/shell via execute_series heredocs.\nRequired paths: rules/README.md, rules/manifest.json (only if absent), rules/run-tests.sh, .github/workflows/rules-validate.yml.\nUse exact content from the BOOTSTRAP FILES block in this SOP. FORBIDDEN: conftest-action, instrumenta/conftest, or hand-written workflow differing from bootstrap. then git commit (verbatim):\n     cd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 git add rules .github \u0026\u0026 git diff --cached --quiet || git commit -m \"codify: sync rules validation scaffold\"\n   - **opa test** failure naming a pack dir: fix `policy.rego` / `policy_test.rego` / fixtures via create_files (absolute paths under /tmp/governance-codify).\n   - **manifest** validation: fix `rules/manifest.json` schema/entries.\n5. Push repair commit — ONE execute_series (substitute CODIFY_BRANCH):\n   cd {{CLONE_DIR}} \u0026\u0026 set -eu \u0026\u0026 BRANCH='{{BRANCH}}' \u0026\u0026 git add -A \u0026\u0026 if git diff --cached --quiet; then echo \"ci_repair_nothing_to_push\"; exit 0; fi \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"{{COMMIT_MSG}}\" \u0026\u0026 git push origin \"$BRANCH\" \u0026\u0026 git rev-parse HEAD\n6. `note(codify_ci_iteration=\u003cn\u003e)` with failure summary; loop to step 1.\n\nFORBIDDEN: parsing `gh pr checks --json` (often empty). Use the CI gate script table output only.\nFORBIDDEN: shell heredocs (`cat \u003c\u003c`) for scaffold files — use create_files.\nAfter 5 failed cycles → `blocked:codify_ci_failed` with last log excerpt. Do NOT merge.\n",
